WEBVTT

00:04:00.278 --> 00:04:01.862
Well, how?

00:04:02.488 --> 00:04:04.323
There’s a lot of ways you could do it.

00:04:04.323 --> 00:04:05.366
You’re not sure how.

00:04:05.366 --> 00:04:09.036
Sometimes it’s easier, frankly,
to just double down

00:04:09.036 --> 00:04:12.123
and keep doing more
of what you’re already doing.

00:04:12.707 --> 00:04:15.251
That might not be the best answer,

00:04:15.251 --> 00:04:16.794
but it’s an answer,

00:04:16.794 --> 00:04:18.296
and it removes uncertainty.

00:04:19.005 --> 00:04:21.882
The picture gets even worse

00:04:21.882 --> 00:04:25.553
when we’re talking
about existential questions;

00:04:25.553 --> 00:04:29.515
when we’re talking
about uncomfortable matters

00:04:29.515 --> 00:04:33.352
that we might not actually
really want to deal with.